== Geography and distribution ==

Christian communities are concentrated in Waribá, Tabakurí, and the main commercial districts. Petran Catholic parishes dominate public religious life, while Burawi Catholic congregations are more localized and remain tied to older colonial-era networks. Protestant churches are smaller and often associated with newer immigrant neighborhoods. Cathar communities are scattered, but they are most visible in mixed urban households and among families with interregional ties.

